comments.body:
@francoischalifour You're talking about this, right?

```js
insightsClient('setUserToken', 'def');

search.EXPERIMENTAL_use(createInsightsMiddleware({ insightsClient }));
```

(To make sure we're on the same page,) user interacts with `insightsClient` to set userToken and the middleware gets updated and set the token into searchParameters. So

> Is there a use case where the Insights' userToken can differ from InstantSearch's?

The answer is "no". And I think it makes sense to add a warning.
